"id": "3b77e4d9-1e36-4062-90c9-06b0758c6b70", "type": "concept", "title": "Functional rehabilitation, interdisciplinary care, and realistic outcome measures"}, {"id": "e300716a-52fa-4ecd-b15d-b65c3e45439e", "type": "concept", "title": "Discharge risk, supply continuity, teach-back, referrals, and follow-up ownership"}]}]}, {"id": "0175008a-895f-4165-a28a-15e2332617ba", "type": "topic", "title": "Diabetes and Glycemic Management", "description": "MNT for diabetes is individualized and coordinated with medications, glucose monitoring, activity, culture, resources, and the person's priorities.", "children": [{"id": "5e8ab471-f078-4ec4-9e9f-0db24ff498e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pathophysiology and assessment", "description": "Students differentiate diabetes types and identify data needed for safe care.", "children": [{"id": "db4e306e-b7ed-43c9-a3c7-215627c1a5d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Type 1, type 2, gestational and secondary diabetes; insulin resistance and deficiency"}, {"id": "c93deaf0-0b34-43a7-94bc-70f3713894f1", "type": "concept", "title": "A1C, glucose patterns, CGM metrics, hypoglycemia, medications, kidney disease, and complications"}, {"id": "5d637747-1267-466b-9dd0-9dfee55fca31", "type": "concept", "title": "Food access, distress, numeracy, work schedule, disordered eating risk, and readiness"}]}, {"id": "bf26d9d6-7d50-4469-bde9-443e9b85b7fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nutrition intervention", "description": "Students use pattern-based and carbohydrate-aware strategies without imposing one universal diet.", "children": [{"id": "66f6fcee-434f-47da-b51f-c97a7d37b768", "type": "concept", "title": "Carbohydrate amount, quality, timing, fiber, beverages, fats, protein, and overall patterns"}, {"id": "52465747-0e4b-4df7-bfab-984755a208c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Carbohydrate counting, plate methods, consistent-carbohydrate approaches, labels, and dining out"}, {"id": "2b092f94-b0f8-48ce-8154-56bf0bb09c2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Insulin-to-carbohydrate concepts, medication timing context, activity, and hypoglycemia prevention"}]}, {"id": "dee12714-aa00-40e5-999c-42f2cf85d998", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monitoring and education", "description": "Students make data meaningful and support self-management.", "children": [{"id": "705f2bf9-386f-4a5d-9045-785fa565c446", "type": "concept", "title": "Collaborative goals, teach-back, problem solving, sick-day and travel planning context"}, {"id": "f3589418-ef84-4424-a105-2a42dc041da5", "type": "concept", "title": "Glucose/CGM response, A1C, lipids, blood pressure, weight/function, and quality of life"}, {"id": "9f28b424-541b-4531-92e9-8e9a40f69675", "type": "concept", "title": "Annual guideline updates, technology access, referral, and interprofessional coordination"}]}]}, {"id": "c683d089-0aa3-4b05-8b25-119526f797aa", "type": "topic", "title": "Cardiovascular Disease, Dyslipidemia, and Hypertension", "description": "Cardiovascular MNT focuses on dietary patterns, substitutions, sodium and potassium context, risk factors, medications, and realistic behavior change.", "children": [{"id": "0a8f0328-9db8-4741-8320-c15e9031da49", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk assessment and mechanisms", "description": "Students connect atherosclerosis and blood-pressure regulation to nutrition-relevant factors.", "children": [{"id": "c3ab3b62-3471-4cd2-91c7-c36537109558", "type": "concept", "title": "ASCVD risk, LDL/non-HDL cholesterol, triglycerides, blood pressure, diabetes, smoking, and family history"}, {"id": "9a8bf3f5-b7e5-4d97-9a1d-09ee5aa8e7cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Lipoproteins, endothelial function, inflammation, sodium–volume regulation, and kidney interaction"}, {"id": "0cddb238-2eba-4c75-b059-2983c8c561a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Social determinants, medication adherence, sleep, activity, and stress"}]}, {"id": "6ab1cf79-8d4f-4ef7-b3de-0f7571733a18", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence-based dietary patterns", "description": "Students emphasize whole-pattern changes and meaningful substitutions.", "children": [{"id": "70488055-34a5-4bcd-8180-eb32c3fe1d35", "type": "concept", "title": "DASH, Mediterranean-style and culturally grounded patterns"}, {"id": "b7c94936-c754-425a-9ab6-bc222cbfce1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Replacing saturated/trans fats, increasing unsaturated fats and soluble fiber, and limiting excess sodium"}, {"id": "9f473c53-4e32-4c7e-8cb2-16b38dcb13fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Potassium-rich foods when appropriate, alcohol context, added sugars, and ultra-processed foods"}]}, {"id": "99c0b1ef-da6d-42f2-9b6e-48940ba1f002", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Counseling and monitoring", "description": "Students translate targets into affordable meals and track clinical response.", "children": [{"id": "ee6bedd0-d98d-45b5-a65f-d6cb8a91cfeb", "type": "concept", "title": "Label comparison, restaurant meals, seasoning, shopping, cooking, and food access"}, {"id": "70b5b56f-52bf-45dd-948c-f3f3dadcb797", "type": "concept", "title": "Blood pressure technique context, lipid trends, symptoms, weight/fluid, and medication effects"}, {"id": "c6c0eb3f-e674-4392-94d5-9dcbef2d9ccc", "type": "concept", "title": "Statin–food interactions, anticoagulation consistency context, referrals, and follow-up"}]}]}, {"id": "cdb8eebf-fa27-462c-9b68-9760ad411736", "type": "topic", "title": "Gastrointestinal Disorders", "description": "GI MNT begins with anatomy, mechanism, symptom pattern, red flags, and adequacy; unnecessary restriction can worsen nutrition and quality of life.", "children": [{"id": "6cdf3c36-9a3d-44a6-a3ca-a8b7358fb40d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Upper GI and functional disorders", "description": "Students relate symptoms to meal size, composition, timing, medications, and behavioral factors.", "children": [{"id": "c66d5c5c-6dbf-41f6-81aa-cb79ba0a8b09", "type": "concept", "title": "GERD, dyspepsia, nausea/vomiting, gastroparesis, and peptic disease context"}, {"id": "b88bd065-b612-4146-94