nts emphasize whole-pattern changes and meaningful substitutions.", "children": [{"id": "70488055-34a5-4bcd-8180-eb32c3fe1d35", "type": "concept", "title": "DASH, Mediterranean-style and culturally grounded patterns"}, {"id": "b7c94936-c754-425a-9ab6-bc222cbfce1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Replacing saturated/trans fats, increasing unsaturated fats and soluble fiber, and limiting excess sodium"}, {"id": "9f473c53-4e32-4c7e-8cb2-16b38dcb13fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Potassium-rich foods when appropriate, alcohol context, added sugars, and ultra-processed foods"}]}, {"id": "99c0b1ef-da6d-42f2-9b6e-48940ba1f002", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Counseling and monitoring", "description": "Students translate targets into affordable meals and track clinical response.", "children": [{"id": "ee6bedd0-d98d-45b5-a65f-d6cb8a91cfeb", "type": "concept", "title": "Label comparison, restaurant meals, seasoning, shopping, cooking, and food access"}, {"id": "70b5b56f-52bf-45dd-948c-f3f3dadcb797", "type": "concept", "title": "Blood pressure technique context, lipid trends, symptoms, weight/fluid, and medication effects"}, {"id": "c6c0eb3f-e674-4392-94d5-9dcbef2d9ccc", "type": "concept", "title": "Statin–food interactions, anticoagulation consistency context, referrals, and follow-up"}]}]}, {"id": "cdb8eebf-fa27-462c-9b68-9760ad411736", "type": "topic", "title": "Gastrointestinal Disorders", "description": "GI MNT begins with anatomy, mechanism, symptom pattern, red flags, and adequacy; unnecessary restriction can worsen nutrition and quality of life.", "children": [{"id": "6cdf3c36-9a3d-44a6-a3ca-a8b7358fb40d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Upper GI and functional disorders", "description": "Students relate symptoms to meal size, composition, timing, medications, and behavioral factors.", "children": [{"id": "c66d5c5c-6dbf-41f6-81aa-cb79ba0a8b09", "type": "concept", "title": "GERD, dyspepsia, nausea/vomiting, gastroparesis, and peptic disease context"}, {"id": "b88bd065-b612-